      "reviewer_concern": "A: make PTB/TinyStories frozen teachers paper-level reproducible",
      "before": "\\subsection{Teacher preparation and eligibility}\n",
      "after": "\\subsection{Teacher preparation and eligibility}\nPTB and TinyStories teachers each combine a six-layer Transformer of width 256 with a six-layer Grassmann branch of width 240, reduced width 64, and lags $\\{1,2,4\\}$; both use dropout 0.1. Source preparation uses seed 42, 20 epochs, batch 32, sequence length 256, and learning rate $3\\times10^{-4}$; all four sources select epoch 20 by validation. Fused teachers use ten joint epochs, freezing branches in epoch 1, branch learning rate $10^{-5}$, weight decay 0.01, AMP, initial $\\alpha=0.5$, and late-$k=1$. Fusion-weight learning rates are $5\\times10^{-3}$ and $10^{-2}$, respectively. Validation selects fused epochs 8 and 10, retaining learned $\\alpha=0.470293$ and $0.599406$ for primary continuations; forced $\\alpha=0.5$ applies to the WikiText-2 controls.\n\n"
